  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 7 original messages plus 1 that arrived while I worked, all closed.\n\n- Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: The August potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample, so it didn't count. I first renewed for 90 days and ordered a repeat BMP. Then a St. Brigid report arrived: a valid potassium of 5.8, collected 10/20. I cancelled the refill. Review task to you (task-t0022), corrected message to the patient, note written. The repeat BMP (sr-t0002) is still ordered.\n- Samuel Price (pt-0030), lisinopril 20 mg and metformin 1000 mg BID (1 patient request + 2 pharmacy requests, handled as one): Metformin renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0006). Kidney function (eGFR) is 58 after correction, and an outside HbA1c of 7.1% from 8/19 is within 6 months. Lisinopril was first renewed. Then the 10/06 creatinine was corrected to 1.49, 35% above the 1.10 before the September dose increase. I cancelled the refill. Review task to you (task-t0023), corrected message to the patient, note written.\n- Marcus Webb (pt-0031), lisinopril 10 mg and metformin 500 mg: Metformin renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0013). The low eGFR of 39 was entered in error and doesn't count. Lisinopril first got 30 days + a BMP order because no BMP was on file within 12 months. A BMP from 10/22 (potassium 4.6) then arrived, so I replaced it with 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0024). Updated message to the patient, note written. I can't cancel orders, so the now-redundant BMP order (sr-t0012) is still open; I sent you a task to cancel it (task-t0032).\n- Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070), lisinopril 20 mg: Not refilled. Creatinine was 1.00 before the 9/28 dose increase and 1.46 on 10/19 (up 46%). The St. Brigid urgent-care creatinine of 1.24 was drawn after the dose change, so it isn't the baseline. Review task to you (task-t0017), focused on his current order mr-70002, which I left active. Patient informed, note written.\n\n**Needs you soon:**\n- **Refill reviews (task-t0017, task-t0022, task-t0023):** Mr. Price and Mr. Kaplan say their lisinopril supply is finished or nearly finished. Mr. Price's and Mr. Odum's previous lisinopril orders were stopped when I placed the renewals, so neither has an active lisinopril order now.\n- **Results queue:** I didn't touch it, as you asked only for messages. It still has 9 open items, including critical potassiums for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4).",
